    description: "FILED 2026-10-01 from WI-mofil-tidog-forob-tovah-givud-lijog-vuvug-gutid (the per-cause sizing of its 622).\n\nMECHANISM. An UNANNOTATED closure parameter -- `ws.onText { ws, string in ws.send(string) }`, `app.get { req in req.query[...] }` -- has no type in the swift binding pass. Its type is the CALLEE's closure signature (`func onText(_ cb: @escaping (WebSocket, String) -> ())`), which nothing records: the return-type registry keys `<Owner>.<method> -> return type`, not the parameter types of a function-typed parameter. WI-mofil bound the ANNOTATED form (`{ (fm: FileManager) in }`) and made a closure a scope; the unannotated form is the larger population and needs this new registry.\n\nSIZED (WI-mofil instrument causes.py, dev 8cfcab7b07, lowercase-hint method sites where _type_of returned None, multi-call lines excluded, same-file declaration search):\n    vapor 142 of 622 (22.8%) . hummingbird 568 of 1,120 (50.7%) . Kingfisher 50 of 542 . Alamofire 50 of 1,190 . swift-argument-parser 30 of 281\nLargest single cause on vapor and hummingbird. NOT counted here: closure SHORTHAND arguments ($0), the same problem with no name.\n\nDIRECTION. Pass 1 records, per in-repo `func`, the parameter types of each function-typed parameter (trailing-closure position first); Pass 2 binds a closure's i-th parameter from the callee row when the callee's receiver is typed. In-repo callees only reach PROJECT types for many of these (Vapor's own RoutesBuilder.get -> Request), which INV-kotob refuses in the module slot; the library-signature catalogue (WI-lalot) would need closure-parameter rows to reach NIO/Foundation types. Size by callee kind (in-repo vs library) BEFORE building. forEach/map/compactMap element binding is WI-bodav, not this.\n\nPRICE ON THE MODULE SLOT AND PRIMITIVES REACHED, not the typed share (INV-kotob, L5). Direction warning as on WI-mofil: more typed receivers feed sanitizer registration."  # b30a
    fields: {}  # b30a
